    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q3",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Describe fully the single geometric transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{A}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; 3 &amp; 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} &amp; 0 &amp; 5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 0 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{B}\"></span>.</p><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> followed by the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span>.</p><p>To determine matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span>, a student attempts the following matrix multiplication.</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &amp; -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 &amp; \\frac{1}{2} &amp; \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 &amp; 3 &amp; 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} &amp; 0 &amp; 5\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 0 \\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) State the error made by the student.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Determine the correct matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{C}\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
