    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q4",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) (a) Show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2 + 3i}{5 + i} = k(1 + i)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant to be determined.</p><p>(Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> is a positive integer</li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{2 + 3i}{5 + i}\\right)^n\"></span> is a real number</li></ul><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) use the answer to part (a) to write down the smallest possible value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) The complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z = a + bi\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z^{10}| = 59049\"></span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arg(z^{10}) = -\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\"></span></li></ul><p>determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
