    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:138mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q05-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figures 1 and 2. Central vertical cross-section of the pile and the shaded region R bounded by the curve and axes.\"></figure><p>A large pile of concrete waste is created on a building site.</p><p>Figure 1 shows a central vertical cross-section of the concrete waste.</p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, shown in Figure 2, has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y + x^2 = 2 \\quad 0 \\leqslant x \\leqslant \\sqrt{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 2, is bounded by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis, the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis and the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>The volume of concrete waste is modelled by the volume of revolution formed when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is rotated through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"360^\\circ\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. The units are metres.</p><p>The density of the concrete waste is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"900 \\text{ kgm}^{-3}\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Use the model to estimate the mass of the concrete waste. Give your answer to 2 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Give a limitation of the model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>The mass of the concrete waste is approximately 5500 kg.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Use this information and your answer to part (a) to evaluate the model, giving a reason for your answer.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
