    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} + \\lambda \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> is a scalar parameter.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> is parallel to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> are perpendicular.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> contains the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Determine a Cartesian equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Verify that the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(3, 1, 1)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the point of intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2, 3, 2)\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(p, q, r)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\sqrt{5}\"></span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p, q\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> are positive integers</li></ul><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) determine the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
