      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q9",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P = \\begin{pmatrix} k &amp; -2 &amp; 7 \\\\ -3 &amp; -5 &amp; 2 \\\\ k &amp; k &amp; 4 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant</p><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P\"></span> is non-singular for all real values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; -1 \\\\ -3 &amp; 0 \\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q\"></span> represents a linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span></p><p>Under <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(a, 2)\"></span> and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(4, -a)\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant, are transformed to the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&#x27;\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B&#x27;\"></span> respectively.</p><p>Given that the distance <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&#x27;B&#x27;\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{58}\"></span>, determine the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
