      "id": "exam/edexcel-8fm0-01-2023-june/q10",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) The quartic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^4 + 5z^2 - 30 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>has roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p, q, r\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\"></span>.</p><p>Without solving the equation, determine the quartic equation whose roots are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3p - 1), (3q - 1), (3r - 1)\\text{ and }(3s - 1)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Give your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w^4 + aw^3 + bw^2 + cw + d = 0\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a, b, c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) The roots of the cubic equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"4x^3 + nx + 81 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span> is a real constant</p><p>are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha, 2\\alpha\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha - \\beta\"></span></p><p>Determine</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) the values of the roots of the equation,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
